+No P0 findings.
+
+1. **P1 — Comparing `version !== PROMPT_VERSION` can downgrade a newer arc during a rollback.** The plan describes “older” arcs but proposes inequality ([plan:79](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/docs/plans/261002g-marginalia-head-in-plain-words-and-every-note-says-where-it-came-from.md:79)). Arc freshness already treats every unequal version as stale ([arc.ts:252](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/arc.ts:252)), and the job stamp requires exact equality ([pipeline.ts:3245](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/pipeline.ts:3245)). Thus an `arc/5` rollback encountering `arc/6` can auto-run and overwrite it with `arc/5`. Quotes already documents and tests the correct rule: parse the numeric version and treat only a strictly smaller, parseable version as outdated ([quotes.ts:981](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/quotes.ts:981), [quotes-find-more.test.ts:101](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/tests/quotes-find-more.test.ts:101)). Put an `isArcOutdated` predicate in the import-free leaf and test older/current/newer/unparseable values.
+
+2. **P1 — The proposed seam needlessly blanks valid content, and `/api/arc`’s “stale” result is semantically conflated.** `ArcFound` says `stale` means the article moved and `outdated` means the prompt changed ([types.ts:948](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/types.ts:948)), but `loadArc` computes `stale` with `arc.isStale`, which also includes prompt and model changes, while separately returning `outdated` ([pg.ts:4124](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/store/pg.ts:4124), [arc.ts:258](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/arc.ts:258)). `useArc` then turns that into `arc = null` and `status = "absent"` ([useArc.ts:118](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/useArc.ts:118)). That removes the arc not only from Marginalia but also Structure’s list face ([Reader.tsx:499](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/reader/Reader.tsx:499), [Reader.tsx:2097](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/reader/Reader.tsx:2097), [Reader.tsx:2464](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/reader/Reader.tsx:2464)). A simpler seam is: keep drawing the payload arc, and when it is strictly older, start one unforced background run directly; the completion callback already refreshes it. That avoids the extra opening GET and the blank interval without worsening today’s payload-freshness behavior.
+
+   Mechanically, the rest of the state machine is sound: an unforced run does regenerate because `stepIsDone` compares the stored stamp with the current prompt stamp ([pipeline.ts:1153](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/pipeline.ts:1153)), and `buildArc` stamps the result with the current constant ([arc.ts:175](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/arc.ts:175)). There is no same-mount loop because `started` is set before the POST and keyed by slug ([useArc.ts:158](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/useArc.ts:158)). A persistent failure retries once per later page mount, not continuously.
+
+3. **P1 — The proposed measurement cannot establish either “plainer” or “fits in three lines.”** Five articles, one old run, one new run, word counts and side-by-side reading ([plan:75](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/docs/plans/261002g-marginalia-head-in-plain-words-and-every-note-says-where-it-came-from.md:75)) omits the project’s required old-vs-old control, blinded pairing, fidelity judgment, and comparison against natural sampling variance ([prompting-guide.md:185](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/docs/project/prompting-guide.md:185)). Also, 20 words do not imply three lines: the column ranges from 200–288px ([layout.ts:518](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/layout.ts:518)), loses horizontal space to padding ([marginalia.css:191](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/styles/marginalia.css:191)), and is clamped by rendered lines rather than words ([marginalia.css:271](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/styles/marginalia.css:271)). The schema accepts arbitrary strings and `buildArc` validates only the number of entries, so “hard cap” is prompt wording, not enforcement ([arc.ts:175](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/arc.ts:175), [arc.ts:278](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/arc.ts:278)).
+
+   Treat 20 words plus rewritten examples as a candidate lever. Run old twice and new once on the same stratified articles; blind part-level pairs for plainness and fidelity; record prompt hashes; and automatically measure both word-limit compliance and actual rendered line count at 200px and 288px. Predeclare pass criteria and include a positive control showing the old prompt fails them.
+
+4. **P1 — The delegated-card design leaves question notes inaccessible by keyboard and touch.** The plan says delegated cards open on keyboard focus and that touch is unnecessary because tapping opens the note ([plan:105](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/docs/plans/261002g-marginalia-head-in-plain-words-and-every-note-says-where-it-came-from.md:105)). But a question is a non-focusable `<p>` with no click behavior ([MarginaliaColumn.tsx:103](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/marginalia/MarginaliaColumn.tsx:103)), while the delegated card deliberately discards touch pointer events ([BlockLinkCard.tsx:447](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/BlockLinkCard.tsx:447)) and opens on focus only when the trigger can receive focus ([BlockLinkCard.tsx:463](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/BlockLinkCard.tsx:463)). The delegated branch is appropriate for the many disclosure buttons; use a controlled `Tooltip` on a button-like question trigger, or explicitly add focus and question-only touch behavior. Otherwise “every note” is false on phones and keyboards.
+
+5. **P1 — Debate headlines are not always third-party/UI, and the existing shared markup cannot express the proposed voices correctly.** `rowWork` deliberately substitutes an AI-derived `workTitle` when the search title is missing or cut short and reports that through `titleIsAI` ([DebatePanel.tsx:1777](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/DebatePanel.tsx:1777)); the Debate band applies `dbt-title-ai` in exactly that case ([DebatePanel.tsx:1923](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/DebatePanel.tsx:1923)). Marginalia must make the same data-dependent choice, not always UI as the plan says ([plan:126](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/docs/plans/261002g-marginalia-head-in-plain-words-and-every-note-says-where-it-came-from.md:126)).
+
+   The implementation also needs explicit per-kind wrappers/modifiers: `.marg-shut-line` is shared by every kind ([MarginaliaColumn.tsx:164](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/marginalia/MarginaliaColumn.tsx:164)); `.marg-open-head` is used for FAQ questions, Debate headlines and citation titles; and `.marg-open-quote` is used for both the article-author FAQ quote and the third-party Debate quote ([MarginaliaColumn.tsx:198](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/marginalia/MarginaliaColumn.tsx:198), [MarginaliaColumn.tsx:229](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/marginalia/MarginaliaColumn.tsx:229), [MarginaliaColumn.tsx:254](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/marginalia/MarginaliaColumn.tsx:254)). Adding those shared classes wholesale to `voices.css` would misvoice another kind.
+
+6. **P2 — A Marginalia branch in `BlockLinkCard` is reasonable, but the plan omits a required styling discriminator.** Adding `[data-marg-tip]` to `SELECTOR` and a `contentFor` arm is not enough: the rendered wrapper chooses `tip-soon` versus `tip-cite` through `CONTROL_SHAPED` ([BlockLinkCard.tsx:163](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/BlockLinkCard.tsx:163), [BlockLinkCard.tsx:523](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/BlockLinkCard.tsx:523)). Marginalia must join `CONTROL_SHAPED` or its `ControlTip` content will be placed in the citation-card styling branch. The existing ARIA behavior is otherwise suitable: it adds `aria-describedby` to non-gutter triggers ([BlockLinkCard.tsx:327](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/web/BlockLinkCard.tsx:327)); pointer-events do not steal the disclosure click; and the `reword` observer is unnecessary while `data-marg-tip` is immutable. The global selector is safe against article forgery because unlisted article `data-*` attributes are stripped ([sanitize-policy.ts:27](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/src/sanitize-policy.ts:27)).
+
+7. **P2 — The proposed tests stop one layer too early for the two silent-success risks.** The hook test can prove that a POST was attempted without proving that the server ran rather than skipped the step, or that the resulting arc carries the current version. Add an integration test with an older stored arc showing: unforced `stepIsDone` returns false, the generated arc has the current version, and the completion refresh becomes ready. Also test newer and unparseable versions do not auto-run, StrictMode/rerenders issue one POST, and failure does not re-arm within the mount. Existing fixtures such as `arc-idle-poll` label a `"test"`-version payload as the current no-network path ([arc-idle-poll.test.ts:88](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbhut48h-marginalia-cutoff-path-origin/tests/arc-idle-poll.test.ts:88)); those must use the exported current constant or they will cease testing what their comments claim. For cards, test actual delayed hover, keyboard focus, `aria-describedby`, exactly one open card, absent native `title`, disclosure toggling, and the chosen touch behavior—not merely that a `data-marg-tip` node can produce markup.
+
+Verdict: **Revise before build—especially the rollback-safe version comparison, keep-old-arc regeneration seam, question accessibility, Debate provenance, and falsifiable prompt evaluation.**
